Here’s the package laid out as it is. I only read files, no git and no gh, and I wasn’t looking for problems.

What it is

@pinkaphant/ecctrl 2.0.4-beta.2. It’s your fork, with Erdong Chen as author and MIT license, and the source headers still point to pmndrs/ecctrl. It’s one package with separate entry points, so a game only imports what it uses:

ecctrl: the character (Ecctrl, in src/character/Ecctrl.tsx) plus its animation states
ecctrl/vehicle: EcctrlVehicle, ShapeCastWheel, ThrustPropeller
ecctrl/input, /camera, /gravity, /time, /curves, /leva, /utils, /animation, /all
example/ is the demo app and public/vehicles.glb is its test car. Neither is part of the library.
How a car works in this package

A car here is a small set of pieces:

<EcctrlVehicle>: one Rapier rigid body, the chassis. It takes normal RigidBody props, so the collider and mass work the same way they do anywhere else in react-three-rapier. carConfig holds the engine: horsepower, max RPM, gear ratios, final drive, auto or manual transmission, steer rate and max steer angle, and torque and steer curves.
Any number of <ShapeCastWheel> children, each placed in the chassis’s local space. Each wheel registers itself with the vehicle through context, so there’s no fixed wheel count and no required names. A wheel holds its suspension (springK, dampingC, rayLength), contact shape (rayShapeR, rayShapeH), role (driveWheel, steerWheel, brakeWheel), grip settings, and visual wheel (wheelModelRadius, with your wheel mesh as its child).
Input: handle.setMovement({ forward, backward, steerLeft, steerRight, brake }), or joystick values.
The handle exposes body, the chassis RapierRigidBody. That’s where anything ecctrl doesn’t cover attaches: doors, hood, wing. Those are your own joints to handle.body, outside ecctrl.
What that means for a car maker

A car maker doesn’t need an engine around it. It needs to output exactly what those pieces take:

the chassis: mesh, collider, mass and center of mass
a list of wheels: position, radius, suspension, and drive/steer/brake role
the engine config
optional extra moving parts, with hinges attached to the chassis
Everything else, including the 60k lines, is outside what a car actually needs here.

